{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1561501-w20-and-power-stat-like-primal-urge-in-wtf","id":1561501,"title":"W20 and Power Stat like Primal Urge in WtF","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-08T22:08:30-07:00","id":1561501,"title":"W20 and Power Stat like Primal Urge in WtF","content":"I restarting a w20 game, and I miss the obvious Primal Urge things that rates from 1 to 10 in chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It brings a sense of evolution and power that is somewhat lacking in Werewolf the Apocalypse. Primal Urge is like, simply a skill.<br /> I would like to house rule something similar, but the idea is also not to break anything. I could call it Gaia's Blessing, or whatever. The name can be cahnge.<br /> <br /> Anyone here has done that already, or has seen something similar with great success ? Any input, hint, reference, or example would be very welcome.<br /> <br /> Thanks guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T00:45:11-07:00","id":1561508,"title":"","content":"I don't recall any specific examples. Though there's the CofD 1e Translation Guide that might have some ideas. <br /> <br /> I think it's probably a lot more work that it's worth considering how spread out the effects Forsaken's Primal Urge covers in the W20 rules. You'd have to alter Rank (severity of frenzies), Rage and Gnosis (points to spend on powers and how many per turn), the WtA Primal Urge Talent (as something that governs special sensory rules), and the healing rules. Then there's the knock on effects on things like Gifts that might not make sense with such alterations.<br /> <br /> WtA is also not tuned for the CofD's default of power stats allowing 6+ traits. The Garou can already get insanely strong with the base 1-5 ratings, shapeshifting, Gifts, Totems, and so on. Letting them get even bigger dice-pools would cause plenty of problems for a long running game; or at least a lot more house ruling as mechanics that assume the RAW scale would have to deal with a suddenly different potential one.<br /> <br /> I do think that the CofD's approach is cleaner and more functional, but I can't help but feel it would be easier to try to run WtA with WtF's rules and go from there than the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T08:33:16-07:00","id":1561522,"title":"","content":"While I agree with Heavy Arms, to not rain on your parade I can suggest a minimalist approach: move WtA Primal Urge from its position.<br /> <br /> This will change a lot of things, but mechanics for it would be simple. Take any other Talent you think that fits to take its place, make Primal Urge work as a distinct stat. Keep all the rules as is otherwise.<br /> <br /> Your greatest challenge will be to determine how Primal Urge increases. I'd suggest either removing XP or keeping at Ability price, but add requisites to get it.<br /> <br /> Primal Urge has distinct roles and mechanics in both games, but has very similar flavor. It is the same concept. Your requisites will reflect what you think that should increase or indicate an increase on someone's innate attunement to the Wolf side.<br /> <br /> Maybe hunting down certain spirits? Umbral journeys? Just behaving like a savage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}